# Performance tripwire for dictionary forwarding across type-rich bodies.
#
# DictAliasTypeStress contains 256 explicitly typed polymorphic functions.
# Each function creates one duplicate Eq predicate (and hence one exact
# dictionary-to-dictionary forwarding binding), followed by 64 ordinary `id`
# applications at a 16-deep Vector type.  The forwarding binding is sparse;
# the rest of the function is deliberately rich in embedded CType nodes.
#
# The old simplifyDictBindings/CSubst path removed each forwarding binding in
# TCheck, but then traversed the whole function and rebuilt every CType it met,
# even though the substitution changed only CVar nodes.  Keeping the tiny
# forwarding binding until LiftDicts lets its already-required traversal
# consume the alias without touching those types.
#
# GHC 9.14.1 calibration for this exact input (three fresh runs per compiler):
#
#                            allocated      max residency
#   LiftDicts forwarding      6.376 GB          81.7 MB
#   legacy CSubst             6.598 GB         140.8 MB
#
# On Linux/GHC 9.14.1, under the explicit RTS settings below, the LiftDicts
# version completed 3/3 runs (126.1 MB capped maximum residency), while the
# legacy implementation exhausted the 160 MB heap 3/3 times.  The heap cap is
# the assertion there; the test deliberately avoids a host-dependent
# wall-clock threshold.
#
# GHC 9.6.7 has a different residency/GC tradeoff: at a 168 MB cap both
# versions complete, even though LiftDicts allocates 429 MB less.  Other GHC
# versions and operating systems therefore use a generous cap.  They retain
# this as a directed compile stress test without pretending that maximum
# residency is portable across RTS implementations.
#
# The source is deterministic generated input and is checked in.  Its complete
# regeneration specification is: 256 functions named stress001..stress256;
# each has the Eq constraint and Vector depth shown above, one `witness = x ==
# x`, and a sequential y01..y64 chain of `id` applications whose last value is
# selected when witness is true.

if { $tcl_platform(os) == "Linux" && [string match "9.14.*" $ghc_version] } {
    set heap_cap {-M160m}
} else {
    set heap_cap {-M320m}
}

compile_pass DictAliasTypeStress.bs \
    "-sim +RTS -H16m $heap_cap -A1m -RTS" 1
